# Third-party provenance -- what is vendored here, what is fetched, and at which commit.
#
# Read this before you update anything: the numbers in docs/ were measured with EXACTLY these trees.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- vendored in this repo
SUPER
  what        : hku-mars/SUPER, the planner this project integrates (ROS 2 package `super_planner`,
                plus `rog_map`, `mission_planner`, `mars_quadrotor_msgs`)
  upstream    : https://github.com/hku-mars/SUPER
  layout      : third_party/SUPER/{super_planner,rog_map,mission_planner,mars_uav_sim/mars_quadrotor_msgs}
  modified    : YES, two patches are baked into the vendored copy and can be re-derived at any time:
                  scripts/patch_super_replan_time_limit.py   (WHTF-REPLAN-TIME-LIMIT, "patch 10")
                  scripts/patch_super_no_backward_head.py    (WHTF-NO-BACKWARD-HEAD,  "patch 11")
                both support --check / --apply / --revert; `bash scripts/check_static.sh` asserts them.
  notes       : `super_planner/log/` (1.3 GB of runtime logs) and any build/ are NOT vendored.

Super-LIO
  upstream    : https://github.com/Liansheng-Wang/Super-LIO
  commit      : f89f48d          ("fix: relocation issue, fixes #29")
  vendored    : third_party/Super-LIO/src/{super_lio,basic}
  notes       : this is the LIO that provides the state the FCU trusts (EK3_SRC1_* = ExternalNav).

livox_ros_driver2
  upstream    : https://github.com/Livox-SDK/livox_ros_driver2
  commit      : 21445540f0d100dc86a7e6df312dd70bbdb4afdf
  vendored    : third_party/livox_ros_driver2

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- fetched, not vendored
ArduPilot (SITL)
  upstream    : https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot
  commit      : dbe792162d06cab66c3475fd5556bf7a120f119e
  why not in repo : ~1.5 GB checkout + several hundred MB of build output
  how         : bash setup/fetch_ardupilot.sh [--build]
  IMPORTANT   : the recorded flights used a SITL build with the truth-tap patch (it is what writes
                tap.csv, the 1.2 kHz ground truth every number in docs/ is scored against).  A clean
                upstream SITL runs the mission but produces no tap.csv, so accept.py cannot grade it.

ROS 2 Humble  (apt)
  sudo apt install ros-humble-desktop ros-humble-pcl-ros ros-humble-eigen3-cmake-module \
                   ros-humble-pcl-conversions libeigen3-dev libyaml-cpp-dev libpcl-dev
